preConditionHook:
// EL: topTail = high - maxlist(open, close), bottomTail = minlist(open, close)
// - low -- the tail AGAINST the direction of the entry (on top for a bull
// reversal, underneath for a bear one). maxlist/minlist select among raw opens
// and closes, the tick-grid price scope their ACCEPTED row allows, so plain
// comparisons stand in for them.
//
// The rule is a permission with an escape hatch: block the entry when the
// opposite tail is large, UNLESS the body is still reasonably strong. That OR
// is why it is carried whole -- the entry pane ANDs, so
// NOT(largeTail) OR strongBody is not reachable from two placements. It is
// also why it is stated positively (fires when the bar is ACCEPTABLE): a
// placement that wants the veto negates it.
//
// Distinct from ReversalBarTailFraction's opposite-tail term, which is an
// unconditional cap with no body override, and from
// SmallBodyLargeOppositeTailBar, which is the conjunction this rule negates.
bodyEdge = open[0];
if (close[0] > bodyEdge) bodyEdge = close[0];
topTail = high[0] - bodyEdge;
bodyEdge = open[0];
if (close[0] < bodyEdge) bodyEdge = close[0];
bottomTail = bodyEdge - low[0];
